// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission1Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2358240220" "The Dead Man's Deck"
// DetailString :
"P864937653" "Mercedes Sheldon hired you to recover an artifact that was stolen from her called the Dead Man's Deck. Mercedes said that her sources reported that the deck might be in the possession of a Longbow agent on the Nerva Archipelago, so you were sent in to persuade some Longbow personnel to tell you who had it. According to a semi-conscious Longbow agent, Officer Martins had been bragging about a poker tournament at the Hook and Anchor for some time, so you figured it was a good bet that Martins had the deck. You walked into the casino and confronted Martins just as accusations of cheating started to fly, an all out brawl erupted around the poker table. You took Martins down and learned that the deck was purchased from Darrin Wade. Upon returning the deck to Mercedes Sheldon you both discovered that the deck was a fake."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Mission2Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P3129900730" "Mercedes Sheldon hired you to recover an artifact that was stolen from her called the Dead Man's Deck. Mercedes said that her sources reported that the deck might be in the possession of a Longbow agent on the Nerva Archipelago, so you were sent in to persuade some Longbow personnel to tell you who had it. According to a semi-conscious Longbow agent, Officer Martins had been bragging about a poker tournament at the Hook and Anchor for some time, so you figured it was a good bet that Martins had the deck. You walked into the casino and confronted Martins just as accusations of cheating started to fly, an all out brawl erupted around the poker table. You took Martins down and learned that the deck was purchased from Darrin Wade. Upon returning the deck to Mercedes Sheldon you both discovered that the deck was a fake.<br><br>Mercedes was not happy with Darrin. She sent you to persuade Darrin Wade to cough up the real deck, or you would rearrange his face. Unfortunately, Darrin was very cooperative, and didn't have the deck. He explained that he never received the Dead Man's Deck from Hector, the Warrior responsible for the theft of Mercedes' artifacts in the first place. Darrin did, however, direct you to the Carnival who did have the deck. You snuck aboard a cargo ship and over to the carnival in Paragon City to recover the deck. Inside the carnival you had to confront the queens of each suit and their leader, the Lady of Aces, in order to recover all the cards in the deck. Once collected you realized that Darrin Wade might pay more for the deck than Mercedes.<br><br>But Darrin didn't want anything to do with the deck. Apparently he has had enough of Mercedes Sheldon's scorn, but he did have an idea for you. He suggested that you keep the real powerhouse behind the deck, the Ace of Spades. You took the card and replaced it with a fake and then returned the deck to Mercedes, confident that she wouldn't discover your treachery until it was far too late to do anything about it."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - DeadMansDeckSouvenirClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// tDetailString :
"P3302735407" "As you look down at the Ace of Spades you recall the job that you did for Mercedes Sheldon to recover <color deepskyblue>the Dead Man's Deck</color><br><br>Mercedes Sheldon hired you to recover an artifact that was stolen from her called the Dead Man's Deck. Mercedes said that her sources reported that the deck might be in the possession of a Longbow agent on the Nerva Archipelago, so you were sent in to persuade some Longbow personnel to tell you who had it. According to a semi-conscious Longbow agent, Officer Martins had been bragging about a poker tournament at the Hook and Anchor for some time, so you figured it was a good bet that Martins had the deck. You walked into the casino and confronted Martins just as accusations of cheating started to fly, an all out brawl erupted around the poker table. You took Martins down and learned that the deck was purchased from Darrin Wade. Upon returning the deck to Mercedes Sheldon you both discovered that the deck was a fake.<br><br>Mercedes was not happy with Darrin. She sent you to persuade Darrin Wade to cough up the real deck, or you would rearrange his face. Unfortunately, Darrin was very cooperative, and didn't have the deck. He explained that he never received the Dead Man's Deck from Hector, the Warrior responsible for the theft of Mercedes' artifacts in the first place. Darrin did, however, direct you to the Carnival who did have the deck. You snuck aboard a cargo ship and over to the carnival in Paragon City to recover the deck. Inside the carnival you had to confront the queens of each suit and their leader, the Lady of Aces, in order to recover all the cards in the deck. Once collected you realized that Darrin Wade might pay more for the deck than Mercedes.<br><br>But Darrin didn't want anything to do with the deck. Apparently he has had enough of Mercedes Sheldon's scorn, but he did have an idea for you. He suggested that you keep the real powerhouse behind the deck, the Ace of Spades. You took the card and replaced it with a fake and then returned the deck to Mercedes, confident that she wouldn't discover your treachery until it was far too late to do anything about it.<br><br>After returning the deck, sans the Ace of Spades, to Mercedes Sheldon you were rewarded as she promised. As you'd hoped she was more fixated on Darrin's treachery or that of the Carnival than on the possibility that you would pull a fast one on her."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission1 
